NAME
    uniq - filter or count adjacent duplicate lines

SYNOPSIS
    uniq [-c] [-D] [-w <chars>] [text...]

DESCRIPTION
    Processes piped standard input (or trailing literal [text...]) and
    collapses consecutive identical lines to a single line. Non-adjacent
    duplicates are not merged; pipe through sort(1) first for global
    deduplication.

OPTIONS
    -c  Prefix each output line with its consecutive repetition count
        and a space. Cannot be combined with -D.
    -D  Print every line belonging to a run of two or more adjacent
        duplicates, omitting unique lines. Cannot be combined with -c.
    -w <chars>, -w<chars>
        Compare only the first <chars> characters of each line when
        detecting duplicates. The first line of each run is kept.

EXAMPLES
    watch log 1 | sort | uniq -c
    rom hash -r --comparable /Games | sort | uniq -D -w 40

EXIT STATUS
    0   Output produced.
    1   Invalid -w count, or -c and -D specified together.

SEE ALSO
    sort(1), wc(1), grep(1)
